WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.282
A video won't rescue a weak page.

2
00:00:03.332 --> 00:00:08.218
But a good explainer, placed well and described properly, can help your page get found.

3
00:00:09.218 --> 00:00:12.037
Search engines want pages that answer the question.

4
00:00:12.087 --> 00:00:16.903
A clear explainer helps, and it can show up in video results and on YouTube.

5
00:00:16.953 --> 00:00:19.517
But it never guarantees a ranking boost.

6
00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:25.495
Put each explainer on the page whose topic it explains, and place it where people see it.

7
00:00:25.545 --> 00:00:28.272
A video buried at the bottom is easy to miss.

8
00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:32.626
Search engines read text, not pictures.

9
00:00:32.676 --> 00:00:38.154
Give the video a descriptive title, and tidy your speaker notes into a short transcript below it.

10
00:00:39.654 --> 00:00:43.309
Add video structured data, or check your platform does.

11
00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:48.605
Keep the page fast with sensible hosting, and use captions and a transcript together.

12
00:00:50.054 --> 00:00:52.908
Your sales deck already explains the topic.

13
00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:57.623
On Pro, a.i. directs the video, tightening the story and designing each scene.

14
00:00:57.673 --> 00:01:00.794
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

